  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the presence or absence of a sure outcome (100% probability outcome) in each lottery. As established, neither lottery has a sure outcome, so the reason would not discriminate between them. The individual, however, based their decision on the maximum possible payoff (4000 > 3000), which is unrelated to the concept of a sure outcome. The information considered by the individual (maximum payoff) does not overlap with the information required by the decision reason (presence of 100% probability outcomes). Furthermore, the justification—choosing based on the highest possible gain—does not align with the rule of the decision reason, which would favor a lottery lacking a sure outcome (a structural feature not mentioned or implied). There is no evidence in the verbal report that the individual considered whether any outcome was certain. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
